---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { Code } from 'astro-expressive-code/components';

const vueExample = `<script setup lang="ts">...</script>

<template lang="nmbl">
div#app
  header.site-header
    h1 {{ title }}
    nav
      a(href="/home") Home
      a(href="/about") About

  main.content
    article(v-for="post in posts" :key="post.id")
      h2 {{ post.title }}
      p {{ post.excerpt }}
      button(@click="viewPost(post.id)") Read More

  footer
    p © 2024 My Site
</template>

<style scoped>...</style>
`;

const viteConfigExample = `import { defineConfig } from 'vite';
import vue from '@vitejs/plugin-vue';
import nmbl from '@nmbl-lang/vite-plugin';

export default defineConfig({
  plugins: [
    nmbl(),  // must be before vue()
    vue(),
  ],
});`;

const tsconfigExample = `{
  "compilerOptions": {
    // ... your existing options
  },
  "vueCompilerOptions": {
    "plugins": ["@nmbl-lang/vue-language-plugin"]
  }
}`;

const installExample = `# Using npm
npm install --save-dev @nmbl-lang/vite-plugin @nmbl-lang/vue-language-plugin

# Using bun
bun add -d @nmbl-lang/vite-plugin @nmbl-lang/vue-language-plugin

# Using pnpm
pnpm add -D @nmbl-lang/vite-plugin @nmbl-lang/vue-language-plugin`;
---

<template lang="nmbl">
BaseLayout(title="Vue Integration Guide")
  section.guide-hero
    .container
      .breadcrumb
        | <a href="/guides">Guides</a> / Vue
      h1 Vue Integration
      p.lead Use NMBL templates with Vue.js

  section.guide-content
    .container
      .content-grid
        aside.toc
          h3 Contents
          nav
            a(href="#installation") Installation
            a(href="#configuration") Configuration
            a(href="#basic-usage") Basic Usage
            a(href="#intellisense-features") Intellisense Features
            a(href="#troubleshooting") Troubleshooting

        .prose
          div:md
            ## Installation

            To use NMBL in Vue projects, you need the Vite plugin (for compilation) and the Vue language plugin (for IDE intellisense):

          Code(code={installExample} lang="bash")

          div:md
            ## Configuration

            ### Vite Config

            Add the NMBL plugin to your `vite.config.ts`. It must be listed **before** the Vue plugin:

          Code(code={viteConfigExample} lang="ts" meta={'title="vite.config.ts"'})

          div:md
            ### TypeScript Config

            Add the NMBL plugin to your `tsconfig.json` to enable intellisense:

          Code(code={tsconfigExample} lang="json" meta={'title="tsconfig.json"'})

          div:md
            ### VS Code Setup

            The NMBL VS Code extension provides syntax highlighting (not yet on the marketplace — install it from the repo). Vue intellisense works through the Vue - Official extension (Volar).

            ## Basic Usage

            Add `lang="nmbl"` to your Vue template block, then write the markup as NMBL:

          Code(code={vueExample} lang="vue" meta={'title="App.vue"'})

          div:md
            ## Intellisense Features

            With the Vue language plugin installed, you get full intellisense support:

          .features-grid
            .feature
              h4 🔍 Go to Definition
              p Click on variables, methods, or components to jump to their definitions
            .feature
              h4 💡 Auto-completion
              p Get suggestions for props, events, directives, and component names
            .feature
              h4 🔗 CSS Class Linking
              p Ctrl/Cmd+click on classes to jump to their CSS definitions (scoped styles only)
            .feature
              h4 ❗ Error Highlighting
              p See TypeScript and Vue compiler errors directly in your template
            .feature
              h4 📝 Hover Information
              p Hover over variables and components to see type information
            .feature
              h4 ♻️ Refactoring
              p Rename variables and have them update across template and script

          div:md
            ## Troubleshooting

          .troubleshooting:md
            ### Variables marked as unused

            Make sure the Vue language plugin is properly configured in your `tsconfig.json` and restart your IDE.

            ### No component auto-import suggestions

            Currently, you need to type the full component name first. Auto-import will then suggest adding the import statement. This experience is being improved.

            ### CSS classes not linking to styles

            This only works with `<style scoped>` blocks. This is a Vue/Volar limitation that applies to all template languages, not just NMBL.

            ### Syntax errors with indentation

            Ensure your template starts at column 0 with no leading whitespace. NMBL uses indentation for structure, so the root element must not be indented.

            ### Template not compiling

            Check that you have `@nmbl-lang/vite-plugin` installed and listed **before** `@vitejs/plugin-vue` in your Vite config.

          .next-steps
            h2 Next Steps
            .next-links
              a.next-link(href="/playground")
                span Try the Playground
                <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
                <polyline points="9 18 15 12 9 6"></polyline>
                </svg>
              a.next-link(href="https://github.com/theoephraim/nmbl/tree/main/examples/vue" target="_blank")
                span View Example Project
                <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
                <path d="M18 13v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6"></path>
                <polyline points="15 3 21 3 21 9"></polyline>
                <line x1="10" y1="14" x2="21" y2="3"></line>
                </svg>
</template>

